# Architecture

```text
src
└── {{ package_slug }}
    └── version.py   __version__
extension
├── __init__.py             register / unregister
├── blender_manifest.toml   the extension manifest
├── operators.py
├── panel.py
└── preferences.py
scripts/build_extension.py  assembles and builds the zip
```

`src/{{ package_slug }}` is the Python package, importable outside Blender. `extension/`
is the add-on Blender loads, and may import `bpy` freely.

## The zip

`scripts/build_extension.py` copies `extension/` into `build/extension/`, builds a wheel
of the package and of every locked dependency (`uv export`) into its `wheels/` folder,
writes the list into `blender_manifest.toml` (at the line `# The wheels are added by
...`), and has Blender pack it (`blender --command extension build`). The dependencies
must be pure Python, and the manifest version must equal `VERSION`, or the build stops.

The targets come from [sowwic/makefiles](https://github.com/sowwic/makefiles)
(`dcc/blender`), fetched into `.make/` and committed; `make update-make` fetches them
again.
